-- title:
--   Uₚ lies in the image of Ψ for p ∥ N
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, let $p$ be an odd prime with $p \in \mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual representation over $k$ (a two-dimensional $k$-space $V$ with a multiplicative action of $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ trivial on the Galois group of some finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$) that is absolutely irreducible, in the sense that its base change to $\overline{k}$ has no invariant subspace other than $\bot$ and $\top$. Let $S_0 \subseteq S$ be finite sets of primes with $p \in S$, and $N \neq 0$ an integer all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$ and outside $S_0$, with $p^2 \nmid N$, and subject to the local conditions: $\bar\rho$ is unramified at each $q \in S$ with $q \neq p$, $q \nmid N$; for each prime $q \neq p$ with $q \parallel N$, $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$ and every inertia element at $q$ has characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$; for each prime $q \neq p$ with $q^2 \mid N$ one has $q^3 \nmid N$ and the same unipotence on inertia at $q$; and if $p \mid N$ then $\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$, i.e. over every valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at $p$ there is a line spanned by a basis vector, stable under the decomposition group, containing $\rho(\sigma)v - v$ for all inertia $\sigma$ and all $v$. Assume the weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ are spanned over $\mathbb C$ by forms with integral $q$-expansions, and let $\theta'$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra generated by the $T_\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S_0$ and the $U_q$ with $q \mid N$, $q \notin S_0$) to $k$, satisfying: $\mathrm{charpoly}(\bar\rho(\sigma)) = X^2 - \theta'(T_\ell)X + \ell$ for every prime $\ell \neq p$ with $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S_0$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$ for a valuation subring lying over $\ell$; $\theta'(U_q) = 0$ whenever $q^2 \mid N$, $q \notin S_0$; $\theta'(U_q)$ equals the trace of the endomorphism induced by $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ on the inertia coinvariants $V/\sum_{\tau \in I_P}\mathrm{range}(\bar\rho(\tau)-1)$ at $q$ whenever $q \parallel N$, $q \notin S_0$; and, if $p \nmid N$ and $p \notin S_0$, $\theta'(T_p)$ equals the corresponding trace on the inertia coinvariants at $p$. Let $\theta$ be the composite of the inclusion [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) $\to$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) with $\theta'$, and let $\Psi$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) to [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S₀ 𝒪 θ'`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) compatible with the canonical maps [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.π`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L151) from the respective Hecke algebras. Assume finally $p \mid N$ and that $\theta'(U_p)$ is the trace of the endomorphism induced by $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ on the inertia coinvariants at $p$, for every valuation subring over $p$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ there. Then the image of $U_p$ under [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.π N S₀ 𝒪 θ'`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L151) lies in the image of $\Psi$.
--
--   This is the case $\ell = p$ with $p \parallel N$ of the assertion that the operators at the primes removed in passing from $S$ to $S_0$ are redundant after localisation at the maximal ideal cut out by $\bar\rho$: in the ordinary situation $U_p$ is recovered from the smaller Hecke algebra, its eigenvalue being the unit root of the Frobenius polynomial. It is one of the components in the proof that $\Psi$ is bijective, as used by [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.bijective_of_subset_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.bijective_of_subset_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq).
